---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Base
  title="About — munfam"
  description="Cloud infrastructure, Kubernetes, and building things that run at zero cost."
>
  <main class="wrap">
    <section class="about">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>munfam</h1>

      <div class="about-body">
        <p class="lede">
          I'm Kelvin Mun. I work in cloud infrastructure and live in Singapore.
          Most days that means backup and data protection at scale; the rest of
          the time it means a Kubernetes lab on a laptop and an unreasonable
          number of half-finished side projects.
        </p>

        <p>
          I write here because the interesting part of infrastructure is rarely
          the install command. It is what happens six months later, when the free
          tier expires, the certificate rotates, or the person who set it up has
          moved on.
        </p>

        <h2>What I work on</h2>
        <dl class="fact-grid">
          <dt>Day job</dt>
          <dd>Cloud and data protection, Veeam</dd>
          <dt>Side projects</dt>
          <dd>Bilingual writing tools for Singapore schools, small web apps, too many Terraform modules</dd>
          <dt>Stack</dt>
          <dd>Kubernetes, AWS EKS, Postgres, Python, TypeScript, Astro</dd>
          <dt>Local setup</dt>
          <dd>Mac, OrbStack, a k3s cluster that exists purely to be broken</dd>
        </dl>

        <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
        <p>
          <a href="https://github.com/munfam">GitHub</a> ·
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/munkelvin/">LinkedIn</a> ·
          <a href="mailto:kelvin.mun@veeam.com">Email</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
